2-21T02:50:49Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in Godot 4.6 beta 1\n- Reproducible in Godot 4.6 beta 2\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Godot Engine v4.6.beta2.official.551ce8d47 -  D3D12 12_0 - Forward+ - Using Device #0: NVIDIA - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn the stable version of Godot 4.5.1, when selecting a resource, a hand icon would appear as if it were an HTML link. Now in Godot 4.6, the hand icon doesn't appear, and when you click, the resource is automatically added to the inspector, but in reality, it isn't added, as shown in the video below. It only adds it after a double-click. It was much better before, where the mouse displayed the hand icon and a single click added the resource, and even then, if you adopt this behavior, it's incorrect, because you can't add it with one click and then, behind the scenes, not actually add it.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b6370123-c427-48ee-abc5-682d9437a606\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nAdd a node like AudioStreamPlayer3D and select a stream for it. If you click on the resource once, it will automatically appear in the stream inspector, but this is incorrect and unexpected behavior.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[godot-project.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24263913/godot-project.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Saulo-de-Souza","id":17336909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzM2OTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17336909?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saulo-de-Souza","html_url":"https://github.com/Saulo-de-Souza","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saulo-de-Souza/followers","following_url":"https://api